 {"id": "PERF-004", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "title": "CLI pays tsx on-the-fly compile every invocation: precompiled dist recall 4.19s -> 3.10s (1.35x); S3/AWS-SDK loaded on read paths", "created_at": "2026-09-28T16:56:06+00:00", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "# PERF candidate: CLI startup pays tsx on-the-fly compilation\n\n## Measurement (same command, same input scale, same box, loadavg ~10-12)\n\nWorkload: `duckbrain recall --namespace coding-hermes --limit 5`\n(ns = 19,888 jsonl chunk files, ~245k live rows, 6.6 GB corpus)\n\n| arm | mean | user | sys |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A: CLI via tsx (production `bin/duckbrain.js` path) | 4.194s +- 0.139 | 3.002s | 1.578s |\n| B: same recallTool, precompiled dist/ (no tsx) | 3.096s +- 0.068 | 1.935s | 1.256s |\n\n`hyperfine --warmup 2 --runs 10 'node /tmp/perf-recall-direct.js' 'node /tmp/perf-recall-dist.js'`\n\nDecomposition (module-census via Module._load hook, and boot ladder):\n- `node bin/duckbrain.js status` (CLI + tool graph, no big scan): 913ms +- 24ms\n- node + tsx only: 38ms\n- node + tsx + require(src/mcp/tools/recall): 566ms +- 18ms  (465 module loads, ~1.6s cumulative self-time)\n- same require via dist/ (no tsx): ~90ms (inferred: dist boot 3.096 vs tsx boot 3.638 for identical tool work ~2.85-2.9s)\n\nEvidence file: /tmp/perf-modcensus.js output — biggest load costs:\n  recall.ts 238ms, duckdb/queries 125ms, serialization/namespaceWriter 120ms\n  (-> git/autocommit 103ms -> s3 99ms -> @aws-sdk/client-s3 91ms), zod 59ms\n\n## Findings\n\n1. Every CLI invocation recompiles the TS module graph with tsx on the fly:\n   ~0.5-1.1s per invocation, ~15-25% of end-to-end recall latency. There is a\n   tsconfig.json (noEmit-style) and NO build script; bin/duckbrain.js\n   hardcodes `require('tsx/cjs')` and TS sources. dist/ compiled fine\n   (tsc exit 0) and passes the same workload.\n2. Read-only recall transitively loads the S3 subtree\n   (queries.ts -> namespaceWriter.ts -> git/autocommit.ts -> s3 ->\n   @aws-sdk/client-s3). Stubbing the s3 resolution cuts module load\n   262ms -> 243ms at tool level; the AWS SDK is never used by a read path.\n   (Lazy-loading s3 inside autocommit is the natural fix.)\n3. Both effects compound for the MCP/HTTP daemons only at boot; the CLI pays\n   per-invocation.\n\nUNVERIFIED: daemon boot amortization (out of scope this tick); interaction\nwith PERF-003 (two-scan fusion is separate and still pending).", "ci_result": null, "guard_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "review_notes": null, "blocked_reason": null, "files_changed": [], "commit_hash": null, "detail": {"fingerprint": "15e958a8b3deda683b2067639e5e4895e46cb75ed18fea433ccd947a1bc4919d", "evidence": [{"run_id": "duckbrain-perf-2026-09-28-tsx-startup", "ts": "2026-09-28T16:56:06+00:00"}]}, "capability_tags": [], "updated_at": "2026-09-28T16:56:06+00:00", "worker_status": "pending", "attempts": 0, "foreman_note": null}
